      "tr": "Dersteki gibi: `sorted(aa_gaps)[int(0.95 * len(aa_gaps))]`.",
      "en": "As in the lesson: `sorted(aa_gaps)[int(0.95 * len(aa_gaps))]`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Fark eksi olabilir (yeni model daha kötü); karşılaştırmada `abs(diff)` kullan.",
      "en": "The difference can be negative (the new model is worse); use `abs(diff)` in the comparison."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\ndef ab_verdict(diff, aa_gaps):\n    ordered = sorted(aa_gaps)\n    band = round(ordered[int(0.95 * len(ordered))], 3)\n    if abs(diff) > band:\n        return [\"real\", band]\n    return [\"noise\", band]\n\n\ngaps = [0.005 * i for i in range(20)]\nprint(ab_verdict(0.136, gaps))\nprint(ab_verdict(-0.05, gaps))\nprint(ab_verdict(0.2, gaps))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\ndef ab_verdict(diff, aa_gaps):\n    ordered = sorted(aa_gaps)\n    band = round(ordered[int(0.95 * len(ordered))], 3)\n    if abs(diff) > band:\n        return [\"real\", band]\n    return [\"noise\", band]\n\n\ngaps = [0.005 * i for i in range(20)]\nprint(ab_verdict(0.136, gaps))\nprint(ab_verdict(-0.05, gaps))\nprint(ab_verdict(0.2, gaps))\n```"
